Keeps the ~36-repo fleet from silently losing work — git housekeeping framed as data-loss avoidance.

Git housekeeping across the ~36-repo fleet, done on demand when Peter feels it needs it. The framing: **housekeeping is mostly about avoiding data loss** — surfacing and clearing the risks `all-repos-status` alone doesn't make obvious, in order of volatility: local uncommitted work (highest risk), stashes (recoverable but invisible), and orphaned remote branches (pushed but with no open PR, holding commits not in `main`). House tools `all-repos-status`/`reposcheck` and `sync-repos.sh` catch uncommitted/unpushed; stashes and ahead/behind on orphaned branches are checked by hand.
